    <label xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="doc_ehm_serialOrLotCode" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/documentation" xml:lang="en">Is this item tracked by serial numbers or lot numbers? A serial number is usually a unique number assigned to a single; a lot or batch number is provided when a batch of items is fungible but must be differentiated from similar items from other batches. Enumerated indicator for serial or lot items. Enumeration are: serial, lot, other, neither. If not included within the class, neither is assumed.</label>
